{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
  "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (John D. Cline)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress placed the phrase \"with respect to its stock\" in Section 301(a) of the Internal Revenue Code to make clear that the taxation rules in Section 301(c) do not apply to corporate payments that a shareholder receives in a nonshareholder capacity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask you a question which is going to come up sooner or later? And it's kind of a threshold question. So, if I may, let me interrupt you with it now. You emphasize the significance of the limiting condition \"with respect to the stock.\" But before you get to that phrase, Section 301 refers to a distribution by the corporation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And again, the Government uniformly takes the position that a controlling shareholder, such as Mr. Boulware, can't embezzle from his own corporation, which is essentially the position that we're taking here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I also wanted to know whether there is in the record the corporation's balance sheet? It was frankly hard for me to believe that this was not in excess of basis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm less concerned with the word \"distribution\" in the statute than I am with the phrase \"with respect to its stock\" -- \"distribution made by a corporation to a shareholder with respect to its stock.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government (as presented by Respondent Ms. Maynard)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the Government here believes that the correct test is the rule of the Ninth Circuit, Your Honor. The Government believes that before a defendant may present a return of capital defense to the jury, there must be some evidence that the corporation intended, as objectively inferred from all the facts and circumstances, to make a distribution with respect to its stock at the time the funds were taken."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Defendant must point to some factual evidence to support three elements: First, that there was a distribution with respect to stock. Second, that the corporation lacked earnings and profits during the relevant tax years. And, third, that the Defendant had a sufficient basis in his stock to cover the funds received."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: At the time -- is it important for the tax treatment that at the time of the distribution it be intended to be either a return of capital or dividends? Does that make the difference as to whether you're going to be able to tax it or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: He said in his proffer that he would present expert testimony that this -- the corporation didn't have profits and earnings, and therefore it was a return of capital. And the district court said no, you don't get to do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Maynard",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government's position at bottom is that he stole these funds, but that -- but in the criminal case it didn't need to characterize it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cline",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think there was an adequate proffer at page 97 of the joint appendix."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you recognize that he would have the burden? If he said this corporation had no earnings and profits so what I got was a return of capital, it would be his burden to show that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, wait. Doesn't he have to show, still show, that it's with respect to stock?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But doesn't -- doesn't he suffice, on a going forward burden, simply to show that he is a stockholder?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What page in your brief did you say?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: The issue is whether the Government wants to convict more -- more malfeasors or whether it wants to collect more money, and the latter obviously prevails in the cases, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, again, that's a position that the Government argues."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "809007d149a746f9f598accce4594fbea5a12f26e91860225ac4f0c0bf2971b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-809007d149a7-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1509",
      "confidence": 0.0,
